quran[9]{c,v,t}:
  21,73,"We made them leaders, guiding (people) by Our command. And We revealed to them the performance of virtuous deeds, the maintenance of prayers and the giving of charity (alms). And they were (always) Our devoted worshippers."
  21,74,"And (as for) Lut, We bestowed upon him (the wisdom of) judgement and knowledge, and We delivered him from the town whose people used to commit acts of indecency. Indeed, they were shameless people with an evil character."
  21,75,"And We caused him to enter Our Mercy. Indeed, he was among the righteous."
  21,76,"And (remember) Nuh (Noah), when he called (his Lord) long before. So We responded to him and rescued him and his family from the great disaster."
  21,77,"And We helped him against the people who rejected Our Signs. Indeed, they were evil people. So We drowned them all."
  21,78,And (remember) Dawud (David) and Sulayman (Solomon) when they both gave the judgement concerning the crop field when the sheep of a tribe entered into it by night (and destroyed it). And We were witness to their decision.
  21,79,"And We gave its better understanding to Sulayman (Solomon). And to all, We blessed sound judgement and knowledge. And We made the mountains and the birds subservient to glorify (Our praises) together with Dawud (David). And We were the doers (of such things)."
  21,80,And We taught him the art of making (armoured) garments for you to protect you in your battle. Will you then be grateful?
  21,81,"And (We made) the stormy wind (subservient) for Sulayman (Solomon), which pursued its course by his command towards the land which We had blessed. And We are the knower of all things."
